*           login has gone, not only on status 0.  !delete_user returns true
*           for 0, 6, 7 and 8 - the login is deleted in all four and only the
*           PROFILE differs - and the half-removed account (lookup.stat # 0)
*           clears it too, which is the arm every "remove it with
*           DELETE.ACCOUNT" note lands in.  PRE_RELEASE_FIXES.md 65.
* 28 Aug 26 Windows port - a third profile warning (8), for the pair that was
*           left behind AND could not be recorded for reclaim.  6 now says the
*           next restart clears it, because it does.  PRE_RELEASE_FIXES.md 36.
* 27 Aug 26 Windows port - the profile warning splits in two: the directory
*           left behind (6) and the ProfileList registry entry left behind
*           (7), which is the one that moves a recreated account's home.
*           PRE_RELEASE_FIXES.md 32.
* 21 Aug 26 Windows port - ONE CONFIRMATION, and it names what will actually
*           go.  Owner's decision: the directory and the Windows account go
*           together, after a single Y/N, replacing the directory-only prompt
*           (6031) and the separate cross-reference question (6029).  What
*           will go is worked out BEFORE the question - !is_sd_user runs at
*           the top now - so the prompt and the deletion cannot disagree, and
*           a group account is never asked about a Windows account it has not
*           got.
* 19 Aug 26 Windows port - SDSYS accounts, and the account's own voc, are lower
*           case on disk.  PROJECT_STATUS.md 5.12 (a).
* 19 Jan 04  0.6.1 SD launch. Earlier history details suppressed.
